      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T02:23:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Screebo is very similar to Rex, the main difference are:\n1. GPIO:\n   * some gpios are used on Rex but not on Screebo, so I delete the gpio nodes and add these gpios to the unused list.\n   * some gpios are differently used between Rex and Screebo so I delete the original nodes and re-define these for Screebo\n2. ADC: the ADC and temp sensors map are overwrite in `screebo/temp_sensors.dtsi`\n3. Interrupts: deleted some unused interrputs\n4. I2C:\n   * deleted unused sensor i2c\n   * change some i2c devices\n\nActually, I have met this situation when I submitted the Screebo init CL, the CL needs to rebase since CL:4392208 and CL:4392209 merged. See the  [CL comment](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/4416520/comments/5760fff8_e8ca4c63)\n\nThanks for your suggestion, I will copy the `generated.dtsi` and rename it to `gpio.dtsi` for Screebo.\n\nI open a bug b/283010946 for this.",
      "parentUuid": "84e3d862_44f0512d",
